# Social Docker Build

## NPM registry (build)

`apps/social/main.Dockerfile` defaults `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` to the same Liara mirror used by frontend/backend:

`https://package-mirror.liara.ir/repository/npm/`

It also defines `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL` as:

`https://registry.npmjs.org/`

Every builder-stage `pnpm` step (install **and** `pnpm run build`) runs through `.cursor/docker/fallback-registry.sh` with a Corepack cache mount, same as frontend/backend. Without this on the build step, Corepack re-downloads pnpm from `registry.npmjs.org` and fails on restricted CI networks.

Override at build time when needed:

```bash
docker build \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_URL="https://…" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL="https://registry.npmjs.org/" \
  -f apps/social/main.Dockerfile .
```

## CI defaults

- **GitLab** (`social:build` in `.gitlab-ci.yml`): passes `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` and `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL`

Set `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` to override the primary registry. Set `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL` only when the public npm registry is not reachable from the runner.
